935f84974237ddf162addf083ce5fb7bd52488","position":"1795272819940033452-b6f2c75f-0a33-4945-93a7-b30248ac5d72"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"0ab43b97d50f67b4676a2e728ff6f6946d4f135d1f66ba1f451eeedcc64995a2","event_uuid":"4d3db2e3-b9b4-4d8b-9e5e-3f9b7b0b7f37","position":{"commit_sha":"60343974fe99c2f19138b42efbc5c7911e64419c","position":"1795274533425330001-4d3db2e3-b9b4-4d8b-9e5e-3f9b7b0b7f37"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-311_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"05f74084-8156-4489-b43f-fbb9222cdc20","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root-cause evidence (2026-11-21 PST, rebar-session-05f74084). All runs are on tmp/b4-cold-censorable-armedcrab with a throwaway, sweep-windows-only workflow on windows-latest, Git 2.56.1.windows.1:\n- Run 44897234719 (origin/main 863abe7cd19): all 11 store-history tests fail under xdist (10 failed, 1 error), serially with `-p no:randomly` (5 failed + 1 error at that order), and each test alone. So the failures do not depend on test order or interaction.\n- Run 44899637411 (unmodified test file, fsck_restore's run_git logged by a `-p` plugin): `git log --diff-filter=D` finds the deleting commit. Then `git show e6aa6b4...^:328e-301e-fdf4-4369/1795261069748668001-...-COMMENT.json` returns rc=128 with `fatal: failed to stat '<arg>': Filename too long`, and `restore_deleted_sources` returns []. The same test passed in run 44899366277, whose pytest temp path was shorter.\n- Run 44900309390, with fsck_restore reading via `git cat-file blob`: the b636 and 08c8 modules pass (12 passed). In the same run, a probe sent `update-index --index-info` stage lines through text-mode stdin and got an empty index (`ls-files -s` = b''); through bytes stdin it got all 3 stages. That is the unmerged-recovery fixture's failure.\n- Local reproduction is not possible on macOS: a missing first path component returns ENOENT before any length check, whereas Windows rejects an over-long path before the lookup.\n- The other product `git show <rev>:<path>` sites are filed as comic-heavyset-jerboa.","timestamp":1795261703568663001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pre-merge Windows validation: run 44902458156, job 136841032132 'sweep (windows)', on tmp/b4-cold-censorable-armedcrab at 2ffe27b54d3 (the exact change on origin/main 1a11014a3a4, with store-history.args deleted). Result: 5 failed, 20464 passed, 892 skipped in 1:27:25. None of the 11 former store-history lines, nor tests/unit/test_fsck_restore_long_path.py (whose MAX_PATH test runs only on Windows), is among the failures. The 5 failures are the same pre-existing, out-of-class ones that also failed on smoking-bereft-boar's run 44900371740: test_check_verify_host x3 (AF_UNIX, consummate-amethyst-bull) and test_git_metrics x2 (fast-import on Windows).","timestamp":1795268319783866001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"make verify on 2ffe27b54d3 exited 0 (default tier 21650 passed / 32 skipped; integration 226 passed / 2 skipped). The spy tests in tests/unit/test_fsck_restore_long_path.py fail on origin/main's fsck_restore.py (2 failed) and pass with the fix. Pushed as Gerrit 3511 (hashtag rebar-session-05f74084). tmp/b4-cold-censorable-armedcrab has been deleted.","timestamp":1795270543403636001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed. Gerrit 3511 patch set 1 (2ffe27b54d33e98ec3a1c1c5cd69012e112f4839): LLM-Review +1, Verified +1 (gerrit-verify run 44912975195, success), 0 unresolved. Submitted with scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py 3511 --revision 2ffe27b54d3...; merged as 4f14a00093f52f3ecc82d4741326dd17494bad99, contained in origin/main. AC1 waits on the first scheduled test.yml run on main whose head contains 4f14a00093f.","timestamp":1795274533425330001}],"created_at":1795154285311984001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"769a069b-de23-476a-bdca-aeee9ef63a05","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8aa0-2120-5ef3-4750"},{"link_uuid":"af968c04-20ca-4687-ba12-b534a8c56783","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"51c6-9f1d-595b-411f"},{"link_uuid":"b6f2c75f-0a33-4945-93a7-b30248ac5d72","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d21e-c43a-9213-44e0"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nDiscovered while triaging breezy-hogged-mastiff. The 11 entries of `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/store-history.args` belong to this bug. Before this investigation the cause was not established. It is now: there are 2 causes, both reproduced on the Windows runner. Run ids and verbatim output are in this ticket's comments.\n\n## Root cause (verified on windows-latest, origin/main 863abe7cd19)\n1. **Product: `fsck_restore` cannot read a deleted source on a deep Windows path.** `restore_deleted_sources` and `_uuid_fallback` read the pre-image with `git show <sha>^:<ticket>/<event>.json`. Without `--`, git stats every revision argument as a possible filename to rule out ambiguity, and it aborts on any stat error other than ENOENT. Under the sweep's pytest temp dir, cwd plus that argument exceeds MAX_PATH. Git dies with `fatal: failed to stat '<sha>^:<path>': Filename too long` (exit 128), so the blob is skipped and nothing is restored.\n   - This covers all 3 `test_b636_rebuild_history_loss` tests and all 5 `test_fsck_repair_restore_08c8` tests (the rebuild never runs, because the restore cannot complete the log).\n   - A shorter temp path passes, so this depends on path length, not on test order.\n   - Real users with a deep tracker path on Windows hit the same thing: `rebar store fsck --repair-snapshots` cannot restore what legacy compaction deleted.\n2. **Test: the unmerged-recovery fixture never creates the UU entry on Windows.** `tests/unit/test_store_write_unmerged_recovery.py::_git` sends stdin in text mode. Python on Windows rewrites each `\\n` as `\\r\\n`, and `git update-index --index-info` records no entries from those lines. `ls-files -u` is then empty and the fixture's precondition fails (all 3 tests). Bytes stdin records all 3 stages.\n\n## Approach\n- `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_restore.py`: read the pre-image with `git cat-file blob <sha>^:<path>`, which takes only an object name and does no filename-ambiguity stat. Same bytes, same `check=False` / `text=False` handling. Both sites (`restore_deleted_sources`, `_uuid_fallback`). No config key, env var or flag.\n- `tests/unit/test_store_write_unmerged_recovery.py`: `_git` encodes `_in` to UTF-8 bytes and decodes stdout itself, so stdin bytes are identical on every platform. Assertions are unchanged.\n- New regression test, `tests/unit/test_fsck_restore_long_path.py`:\n  - It asserts that both `fsck_restore` reads use `cat-file blob` and never `git show <rev>:<path>`, by spying on `run_git` while restoring a deleted source in a tmp repo.\n  - On Windows only, it restores a deleted source under a cwd padded past MAX_PATH. The real restore must return the file.\n- The other product `git show <rev>:<path>` sites have the same exposure. They are filed as comic-heavyset-jerboa, not fixed here.\n- `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/store-history.args`: remove each line whose test passes in the Windows validation run. If the file ends up empty, delete it and its `@` line in `.github/workflows/test.yml`; `tests/unit/test_windows_sweep_deselect.py` keeps the 2 in step.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_commands/fsck_restore.py\n- tests/unit/test_store_write_unmerged_recovery.py\n- tests/unit/test_fsck_restore_long_path.py\n- .github/windows-sweep-deselect/store-history.args\n- .github/workflows/test.yml (only if the args file is deleted)\n\n## Testing\n- Pre-merge Windows validation: on the exact fixed tree with the lines removed from the args file, push `tmp/b4-cold-censorable-armedcrab`, dispatch `gh workflow run 294845723 --ref tmp/b4-cold-censorable-armedcrab`, and record the run id and per-test outcomes in a comment. Then delete the tmp branch.\n- AC1 evidence (\"passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix\"): the first scheduled `test.yml` run on main whose head contains the merge commit. Its run id and head SHA go in a comment before the close.\n- `make verify` through verify-slot.sh.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every line removed from `store-history.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `store-history.args` is empty and deleted with its reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml`, or each remaining line names a test recorded on this ticket as intentionally unsupported on Windows with the reason.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck_restore.py","reason":"cold-censorable-armedcrab: rev:path filename stat and text-mode stdin on Windows"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_store_write_unmerged_recovery.py","reason":"cold-censorable-armedcrab: rev:path filename stat and text-mode stdin on Windows"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_fsck_restore_long_path.py","reason":"cold-censorable-armedcrab: rev:path filename stat and text-mode stdin on Windows"},{"path":".github/windows-sweep-deselect/store-history.args","reason":"cold-censorable-armedcrab: rev:path filename stat and text-mode stdin on Windows"},{"path":".github/workflows/test.yml","reason":"cold-censorable-armedcrab: rev:path filename stat and text-mode stdin on Windows"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","51c6-9f1d-595b-411f"],["relates_to","d21e-c43a-9213-44e0"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"b226f25c-2f90-4c29-b434-60723f120fc1","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_id":"a2da-e61b-989e-4862","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: 11 store-history restore and unmerged-path tests fail; cause not yet established","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["97da85ac-10ee-4adb-8add-0e4459df1269","861dc466-9fc5-4788-ac58-7ce309a7c043","a69ce9ba-02e2-49a0-a4d3-3fbf671ab3d8","af968c04-20ca-4687-ba12-b534a8c56783","0a18b63a-2727-4f2e-a3a5-9c5982449a15","b226f25c-2f90-4c29-b434-60723f120fc1","e8d32f4a-1811-4a4c-b502-b64daffeddfa","028a5119-b5ad-4d68-878b-6f1e5ecf6f7d","5eb6a012-3768-4ae7-aa2a-9e2554e87f60","b6f2c75f-0a33-4945-93a7-b30248ac5d72","4d3db2e3-b9b4-4d8b-9e5e-3f9b7b0b7f37"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795274533425330002,"uuid":"b2e67c3e-8dcb-48df-815c-122e5fd977d9"}